-       A `Shrink` is a configuration, and applying it does the work:
-       `Shrink(…)(classpath, entryPoints, out)` writes the closed world of `classpath` which
-       `entryPoints` reach to the directory `out`, and gives a `Shrink.Report`.
+       Un `Shrink` es una configuración, y al aplicarlo se hace el trabajo:
+       `Shrink(…)(classpath, entryPoints, out)` escribe en el directorio `out` el mundo cerrado de
+       `classpath` que alcanzan `entryPoints`, y devuelve un `Shrink.Report`.

=       `entryPoints` reach to the directory `out`, and gives a `Shrink.Report`.
